# W9, SIGTERM (ADR-0110 item 4): W8 at -j4 in the background, its pid in a
# file, and SIGTERM to that top make alone, as
# tools/posix-surface/remote/w9_session.py sent it, once a table exists (the
# time TASK-02b's 1.5 s reached; review R1); status 143, a target deleted,
# no partial target and no process left.
#
# The wait for the tables is the runner's, on an event: make writes to the
# terminal, as in w9-int.script, and the kill line is typed once a leaf has
# begun its second table (a job slot came back, so a table is written). The
# guest's loop then only checks that a table exists and ends at once. It
# used to poll from the start of the build: under TCG on one CPU its ls,
# cat and sleep, three processes ten times a second, took most of the CPU
# from the build, whose first table then did not come within the run's
# 600 s (scheduled run 43699859694, candidate run 43686441057).
! -FAIL
! panicked
! ZORAYA-FAULT
< PSURF> 
# The cd on a line of its own: `cd X && make &` would put both in a
# background subshell, whose pid is not make's (review R1's fix).
> cd /work/w9-term\r
% boot
< PSURF> 
> make -j4 2>&1 & echo $! > /tmp/make.pid\r
< ./mktab 2 > t2.h
> until ls */*/t?.h > /dev/null 2>&1 || ! kill -0 $(cat /tmp/make.pid); do sleep 0.1; done; kill -TERM $(cat /tmp/make.pid); wait $(cat /tmp/make.pid); echo W9-STATUS $?\r
< Deleting file 't
< W9-STATUS 143
< PSURF> 
% w9-term
> sh /tests/w9-check.sh /work/w9-term\r
< W9-PARTIAL 0
< PSURF> 
> sleep 0.5; t_posix live 3000\r
< W9-LEFT 0
< PSURF> 
> exit\r
< POSIX-STATS images=
< POSIX-CALLS
< BROKER-STATS
